-- and the other side of the sharpening: two reports on one compound whose values disagree, and one
-- function agreeing with both. The function is the count itself, and what reconciles the reports is that
-- their conditions differ. So a record holding both is not holding a contradiction, and a record that
-- cannot tell this case from the Inventory's -- one substance, one hazard class, one set of criteria, two
-- answers -- is a record whose disagreements cannot be read at all. The first component is the
-- disagreement; the second and third are the agreement of count-of with each report.
cyh-reports-consistent : (a : cr-value Nat cyh-report-300 ≡ cr-value Nat cyh-report-190 → Empty) × ((b : count-of (cr-cmp Nat cyh-report-300) (cr-cond Nat cyh-report-300) ≡ cr-value Nat cyh-report-300) × (count-of (cr-cmp Nat cyh-report-190) (cr-cond Nat cyh-report-190) ≡ cr-value Nat cyh-report-190))
cyh-reports-consistent = (cyh-reports-disagree , (cyh-count-300 , cyh-count-190))
